Adaptation 08-codex-substitutes-not-opus

Added here, not in the fork. Adaptation 07 runs a value that resolves to an Opus model at
`medium`, "whatever that line or a platform mapping says". On Codex a reader sometimes applied
that rule to a Claude alias that the Codex mapping substitutes with a non-Opus model, and ran
the substitute at `medium`. The Codex mapping now says its substitutes are not Opus models, so
each role runs at the level the mapping lists. Since 1.51.5 that level (`high`) is below the
sheet's `default effort` (`xhigh`, which setup-pstack writes), so the mapping says its level takes
that line's place on Codex; a level the role value names with `@` still applies.

Applies to the port's plugins/pstack/skills tree after the patches numbered before it.

diff --git a/poteto-mode/references/codex-tools.md b/poteto-mode/references/codex-tools.md
index a818a68..7136616 100644
--- a/poteto-mode/references/codex-tools.md
+++ b/poteto-mode/references/codex-tools.md
@@ -57,6 +57,8 @@ Skills name Claude defaults (a single-role default for code/prose/judgment, a wo
 - Execution and review panels (`arena`, `interrogate`): use `gpt-6.2-sol` at `high` reasoning. Note reduced model diversity when every participant uses the same model; independent contexts do not provide cross-model independence.
 - Planning (`architect`) and read-only advice: select the host's dedicated planning/advisor route and its effort, rather than an execution alias. Never use that route for implementation or code review.
 
+These substitutes are not Opus models, so the `medium` rule for a value that resolves to an Opus model does not apply to them on Codex. On Codex the level listed above for each substitute takes the place of the sheet's `default effort` line; a level the role value names with `@` still applies.
+
 `/setup-pstack` writes the configured model list. On Codex, set it to your Codex model slugs.
 
